<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:33Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="/atoms/rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Guinea-Bissau votes to reshape presidency</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d38ee92fc62bb770e65a5df49abc398148f2b5de7f2bf00fc7ebae43bf47d93</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:33Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T12:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/guinea-bissau-votes-to-reshape-presidency/a-78562523--6d1dcf4a63cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/guinea-bissau-votes-to-reshape-presidency/a-78562523?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The West African nation's military government wants to amend the constitution to give more powers to the president. The junta, which seized power last year, says it will hold elections in December.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Greece, Turkey clash over protected Aegean marine areas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5068e4eb9fc4ab602e54bf1e8badd02564b9e674fa2ffd5801e1d08b42592312</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:33Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/greece-turkey-clash-over-protected-aegean-marine-areas/a-78550021--198e60df237d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/greece-turkey-clash-over-protected-aegean-marine-areas/a-78550021?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkey has announced the creation of two protected zones in a disputed area of the Aegean Sea, sparking an angry reaction from Greece. Does this mark a new chapter in a long-running dispute between the two countries?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's citizen-led school audits test limits of activism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19ef3e27df9480299eafaf3249d2833a2fc6a77b54eb80b799b274d3e805f88f</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:33Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-citizen-led-school-audits-test-limits-of-activism/a-78545789--41cb1b89184e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-citizen-led-school-audits-test-limits-of-activism/a-78545789?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The student-led "Cockroach" movement is taking its campaign for accountability to government schools, but the activists' methods are encountering growing resistance from authorities.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal issues fresh flood warning as 3,000 still missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe489dd44d861d8fbb73f9c5502b361e2a5db0517c3f1e0d9589884ed5882c16</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:33Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T06:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-issues-fresh-flood-warning-as-3-000-still-missing/a-78561068--69ee48f29b5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-issues-fresh-flood-warning-as-3-000-still-missing/a-78561068?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rescuers are trying to reach dozens of hydropower workers trapped in flooded tunnels, but have been hampered by further rainfall.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian-American heads Trump's planned Caucasus trade route</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e9b52d58b6d5c0913adea9a4ae3117f7aa3914b6cd3ef25688803cb5de9121d1</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:33Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T16:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-american-heads-trump-s-planned-caucasus-trade-route/a-78547064--c9f07c7be30b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-american-heads-trump-s-planned-caucasus-trade-route/a-78547064?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Russian-born businessman heads the investment fund financing the so-called "Trump Route," a planned corridor through Armenia linking Azerbaijan with Nakhchivan. Who is Konstantin Sokolov, and what role does he play?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea leans toward military conscription for women</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c0cb90e0c5ff837dd45dea7621a7bf3a6ba3cddd0ca9817b41ac8067b44da8c</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:33Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-leans-toward-military-conscription-for-women/a-78547426--44a420a33a73.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-leans-toward-military-conscription-for-women/a-78547426?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Facing a population decline, fewer potential service members and calls for social equality to be extended to national military service, Korea is inching closer to breaking the taboo on women on the front line.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia keeps EU, Russia in play ahead of key election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6fdb706f692d3c197467cf64c978bfc0fce8d57772d2f7e0546dc129cc26623c</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:33Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-keeps-eu-russia-in-play-ahead-of-key-election/a-78543495--e8aaa1f77f09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-keeps-eu-russia-in-play-ahead-of-key-election/a-78543495?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Serbia heads toward an uncertain election, President Aleksandar Vucic is balancing ties with Russia and EU ambitions. But growing geopolitical tensions and pressure at home are narrowing his room to maneuver.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What next? Kurds say yes, Druze still say no to united Syria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4a791de33f29622d2fc9f05af74fe31006729a7cd0f407a038ef5a4bf230599</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:33Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T16:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/what-next-kurds-say-yes-druze-still-say-no-to-united-syria/a-78549925--bac6343d7f1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-next-kurds-say-yes-druze-still-say-no-to-united-syria/a-78549925?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Druze minority in Sweida, Syria, is now the only group that hasn't accepted central government authority. How does the end of an independent Kurdish area impact Druze plans for a different, divided kind of Syria?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda: World's 'youngest monarch' dies aged 34</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bccb8e9b548bf60171881d9b01b9dee3f540d71d889c2f2ded336135b0078270</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:33Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T14:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-world-s-youngest-monarch-dies-aged-34/a-78549208--984194d8ba1b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-world-s-youngest-monarch-dies-aged-34/a-78549208?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oyo Nyimba, once recognized as the world's youngest reigning monarch, has died in his mid-30s. As one of Uganda's traditional monarchs, he took the throne of the Tooro kingdom in 1995, aged just 3.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's aging autocrats fight to stay in power</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa60eb4ecc2ded9122c0075d8cdfc879dba66bde23632f90a769677b9721687a</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:33Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T14:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-aging-autocrats-fight-to-stay-in-power/a-78487210--789b3c043ada.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-aging-autocrats-fight-to-stay-in-power/a-78487210?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As some of Africa's longest-serving leaders grow older, they are using different tactics to extend their rule. But age, succession battles and public pressure pose new challenges.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal-Tibet flood deaths pass 500, thousands still missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69a7482292f64beaaeb5cd41cd2a80863c5c31c12f29b8974c7b7558cb3ea5b1</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:33Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-tibet-flood-deaths-pass-500-thousands-still-missing/a-78539559--eaabbfdad3ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-tibet-flood-deaths-pass-500-thousands-still-missing/a-78539559?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Red Cross says more than 93,000 people are affected by the deadly floods and landslides on the China-Nepal border. Rescue efforts were temporarily paused after an overflowing lake threatened to trigger more floods.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's King Harald dies at 89</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3df3f4595812df657b3a261e617acf27a79a76a52dcc53b1d1a371e3987c493</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:33Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T08:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-king-harald-dies-at-89/a-78524572--5cdf5505c67f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-king-harald-dies-at-89/a-78524572?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">King Harald is succeeded by his son, who has taken the name King Haakon VIII, with Crown Princess Mette-Marit now queen.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Protesters set fire to migrant camp in Ceuta</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:baebda259211f2b593f14c92635463b157ee41d623fe0c9dcd384bd785440482</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:33Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T00:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/protesters-set-fire-to-migrant-camp-in-ceuta/a-78538847--4bc5545d875d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/protesters-set-fire-to-migrant-camp-in-ceuta/a-78538847?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The unrest comes one month after a mass influx of migrants from Morocco to the Spanish exclave in North Africa.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
